[gd_scene load_steps=5 format=3 uid="uid://cq7k3y0key001"]

; floating_key.tscn -- Assignment 8's FIRST animation-set item.
;
; "Movement with no rig and no frames: a pickup, door, platform or UI
; element ... an AnimationPlayer clip keying position, rotation or scale."
;
; One Sprite2D. No pivot hierarchy, no frame track, no SpriteFrames, no
; second node to inherit a transform from -- so there is nothing here that
; could be called a rig. The clip keys `position:y` and `rotation_degrees`
; and nothing else, and `godot/tests/test_pickup_clip.gd` asserts that.
;
; **It is decorative.** Nothing collects it. Making it collectible would mean
; a collision layer and a piece of game state, both of which CLAUDE.md puts
; out of scope for this assignment. CHANGE-BRIEF.md revision 8.0.1 says so
; rather than letting the film imply a mechanic that is not there.
;
; **The seam is the CONTINUOUS rule**, which is the one that applies to an
; interpolated track: the value at t = 0 and at t = length must match or the
; wrap jumps. position.y 0 -> 0, rotation 0 -> 360, which is the same
; orientation -- and the test checks the rotation seam modulo 360 rather
; than by equality, because 0 and 360 are equal as POSES and not as numbers.

